  "history": "NH 14 runs down through the western side of West Bengal, from Morgram on NH 12 to the railway hub of Kharagpur on NH 16. Before the 2010 renumbering it was known as NH 60. Along the way it passes the stone and coal country of Birbhum, the Raniganj coalfield, and the old temple town of Bishnupur.",
  "facts": [
    "Was known as NH 60 before the 2010 renumbering.",
    "Passes Bishnupur, famous for its terracotta temples.",
    "Crosses the Mayurakshi river at the Tilpara Barrage near Suri.",
    "Links NH 12 in Murshidabad with the big east-coast highway NH 16 at Kharagpur."
  ],
